<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aeneid"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aeneid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aeneid</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aeneid is a Latin epic poem in twelve books by Virgil, written between about 29 and 19 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aeolians"><span class="enc-name">Aeolians</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aeolians were one of the main divisions of the ancient Greeks, speaking the Aeolic dialect, at home in Thessaly and Boeotia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aeolis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aeolis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aeolis</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Aeolis was the ancient name of the north-western coast of Anatolia and the island of Lesbos, settled by Aeolian Greeks from the 11th century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aerial-bombardment"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aerial-bombardment.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aerial bombardment</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Aerial bombardment is the use of aircraft to drop bombs or other munitions on military or civilian targets.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aeschines"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aeschines.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aeschines</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aeschines was an Athenian orator and statesman, the chief political opponent of Demosthenes.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedi