-snip">Agathocles was the eldest son of Lysimachus, king of Thrace, Macedon and western Asia Minor, and a successful commander for his father.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/agathocles-of-syracuse"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/agathocles-of-syracuse.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Agathocles of Syracuse</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Agathocles of Syracuse seized power as tyrant of Syracuse in 317 BCE and later took the title of king.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/agaw-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/agaw-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Agaw people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Agaw are a Cushitic-speaking people of the northern and central highlands of Ethiopia and Eritrea, among the oldest inhabitants of the region.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/age-of-discovery"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/age-of-discovery.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Age of Discovery</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Age of Discovery refers to the period from the fifteenth to the seventeenth century when European navigators, led by Portugal and Spain, explored oceans and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/age-of-enlightenment.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Age of Enlightenment</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Age of Enlightenment was an intellectual movement of the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries that emphasised reason, science, individual rights and