heti"><span class="enc-name">Aghsartan I of Kakheti</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aghsartan I was king of Kakheti and Hereti in eastern Georgia from 1058 to 1084.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aghsartan-ii-of-kakheti"><span class="enc-name">Aghsartan II of Kakheti</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aghsartan II was the last king of Kakheti and Hereti in eastern Georgia, a vassal of the Seljuks.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aghsu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aghsu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aghsu</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Aghsu is a town in central Azerbaijan, on the plain south of Shamakhi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/agiad-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/agiad-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Agiad dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Agiads were the senior of the two royal houses of Sparta, which was always ruled by two kings at once.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/agila-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/agila-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Agila I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Agila I was king of the Visigoths in Hispania from 549 to 554.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/agilolfings"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/agilolfings.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Agilolfings</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Agilolfings were a noble family that ruled the Duchy of Bavaria from about 555 to 788 and also provided kings of the Lombards.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/agilulf"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/agilulf.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Agilulf</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Agilulf was king of the Lombards in Italy from 590 to 616.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/agios-kirykos"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/agios-kirykos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Agios Kirykos</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Agios Kirykos is the main town and port of the Greek island of Ikaria in the eastern Aegean.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/agios-nikolaos"><span class="enc-name">Agios Nikolaos</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Agios Nikolaos is a town on the Gulf of Mirabello in eastern Crete, Greece, and the capital of the regional unit of Lasithi.</span></a></li></ul>
